    "facts": [
      "Element scroll uses DOM scrollBy, not wheel input.",
      "Selected/foreground-page lifecycle and controlled-browser launch differ from bro background flows.",
      "CLI batch --bail plus native text waits can complete the same workflow in one CLI invocation.",
      "Unknown scroll direction can become a zero-delta operation yet return scrolled:true; bro rejects invalid directions instead."
    ]
  },
  "fix": {
    "owner": "ref input preparation and post-scroll rendering lifecycle; Rust flow composition",
    "changes": [
      "Reuse foreground/frame/target preparation without global browser suppression flags",
      "One scroll, then rendering-frame synchronization; no synthetic scroll event or replay",
      "Structured actual before/after/delta/extent/moved/boundary result, with null boundary for unsupported writing-mode origins",
      "Measure range after scroll handlers, reject disconnected/non-scrollable targets",
      "Ref-only flow scroll step plus read_text preserves refs and batches intermediate UI observations"
    ]
  },
